WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.702 --> 00:00:13.545
Agents run on an AI runtime: Claude Code, Codex, the Gemini CLI, or a model provider you reach with a key. This video shows where you set them up, and how you keep their cost under control.

2
00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:22.463
Open Integrations in the sidebar and pick your workstation. Under AI runtime there is one tile for each program and provider.

3
00:00:23.164 --> 00:00:32.743
A tile says whether the program is installed, with the command to install it if it is not, who is signed in, and whether a key is set and whose key is in effect.

4
00:00:33.442 --> 00:00:40.909
Sign in runs the program's own login on the workstation. Open the link, enter the code, and the account shows Signed in.

5
00:00:41.611 --> 00:00:49.376
For an API provider, click Set key. The key is encrypted in your browser for this workstation, and only its runner keeps it.

6
00:00:52.220 --> 00:01:00.924
Every runtime has one main account, and any number of named accounts. Click Add a named account, give it a short name such as work, and set its key.

7
00:01:02.692 --> 00:01:11.524
Make main swaps a named account with the main one. Nothing is lost, and doing it again undoes it. A project picks its account in its own settings.

8
00:01:12.224 --> 00:01:20.373
Allow projects to use my accounts decides whether projects you are not a member of may spend your named accounts. It is off by default.

9
00:01:21.082 --> 00:01:30.981
For keys the whole organization shares, follow the link to Settings, Model providers. Owners and Admins set the key once, and choose which workstations get it.

10
00:01:31.681 --> 00:01:42.305
Each provider has a monthly cap. You are warned at eighty percent and again at one hundred, and at the cap new runs on the organization key are refused until you raise it.

11
00:01:43.004 --> 00:01:57.617
A workstation that joined later shows Not shared. Share it from a workstation that has the key, without typing the key again. A workstation with a key of its own uses that one instead, and it is not capped. Revoke removes the key everywhere.

12
00:01:58.318 --> 00:02:04.185
Keys never leave your browser unencrypted, and a named account is your own key, so it is never capped.
